{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNXZwu4aSaDRuLcT9wEXK4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→created: 2026-02-03T03:15:00Z\n     3→github_issue: null\n     4→source: https://github.com/krazyuniks/guitar-tone-shootout/wiki/IMPLEMENTATION\n     5→---\n     6→\n     7→# Phase 3: Adapter Implementation\n     8→\n     9→Implementation of three parallel adapter sub-phases that build on the core domain (Phase 2).\n    10→\n    11→## Problem Statement\n    12→\n    13→The core domain layer (`libs/core/`) defines entities, value objects, and port protocols but has no concrete implementations. Phase 3 delivers the adapter layer:\n    14→\n    15→- **3A (Persistence):** SQLAlchemy ORM models and repository implementations for `gts_core` database\n    16→- **3B (Audio):** Audio processing library implementing the `AudioProcessor` protocol\n    17→- **3C (Frontend):** Astro build system for templates and static assets\n    18→\n    19→These three sub-phases modify distinct directories and can execute in parallel:\n    20→- 3A: `apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/` and `infrastructure/migrations/`\n    21→- 3B: `libs/audio/src/audio/`\n    22→- 3C: `frontend/astro/`\n    23→\n    24→## Success Criteria\n    25→\n    26→- [ ] All ORM models with relationships pass protocol compliance tests\n    27→- [ ] Repositories implement all methods from `libs/core/ports/repositories.py`\n    28→- [ ] Alembic migrations create complete `gts_core` schema\n    29→- [ ] Audio processor implements `AudioProcessor` protocol with async support\n    30→- [ ] NAM model loading with LRU caching functional\n    31→- [ ] Loudness normalization (EBU R128) operational\n    32→- [ ] Astro builds successfully to `frontend/astro/dist/`\n    33→- [ ] Tailwind CSS compiles with design tokens\n    34→- [ ] Base Jinja2 wrapper generates valid HTML\n    35→- [ ] Static pages (index, about, login) render correctly\n    36→- [ ] `just check` passes (lint, types, tests)\n    37→- [ ] Wiki documentation updated for all three sub-phases\n    38→\n    39→## Execution Guidelines\n    40→\n    41→### Test-Driven Development (MANDATORY)\n    42→\n    43→**Every story MUST follow Red-Green-Refactor:**\n    44→\n    45→1. **RED - Write failing tests FIRST**\n    46→   - Before writing ANY implementation code, write tests for the story's acceptance criteria\n    47→   - Run the tests - they MUST fail (if they pass, you're not testing new behaviour)\n    48→\n    49→2. **GREEN - Implement to pass**\n    50→   - Write the minimum code to make your tests pass\n    51→   - Run tests frequently during implementation\n    52→\n    53→3. **REFACTOR - Clean up (if needed)**\n    54→   - Improve code quality while keeping tests green\n    55→\n    56→### Archive Reference\n    57→\n    58→Archive code at `../../guitar-tone-worktrees-archive-20260202/main/` provides reference implementations:\n    59→\n    60→| Archive Path | Target | Classification |\n    61→|--------------|--------|----------------|\n    62→| `backend/app/models/*.py` | `apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/models/` | REFACTOR |\n    63→| `backend/app/adapters/persistence/*.py` | `apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/` | REFACTOR |\n    64→| `backend/app/adapters/processing/pedalboard_audio.py` | `libs/audio/src/audio/processing/` | REFACTOR |\n    65→| `backend/app/adapters/processing/nam_loader.py` | `libs/audio/src/audio/processing/` | REFACTOR |\n    66→| `backend/app/adapters/processing/ir_loader.py` | `libs/audio/src/audio/processing/` | REFACTOR |\n    67→| `astro/astro.config.mjs` | `frontend/astro/` | REFACTOR |\n    68→| `astro/src/styles/global.css` | `frontend/astro/src/styles/` | REFACTOR |\n    69→| `astro/src/layouts/` | `frontend/astro/src/layouts/` | REFACTOR |\n    70→| `astro/src/pages/*.astro` | `frontend/astro/src/pages/` | REFACTOR |\n    71→\n    72→### Container Execution\n    73→\n    74→All commands run in containers via `just`:\n    75→- Backend: `docker compose exec backend <command>`\n    76→- Astro: `just build-astro` or `just watch-astro`\n    77→- Tests: `just tdd <path>`\n    78→\n    79→### Background Agents\n    80→\n    81→Use `Task` tool with `run_in_background: true` for parallel work:\n    82→- `Explore` agent for codebase research\n    83→- `Bash` agent for running tests in background\n    84→\n    85→---\n    86→\n    87→## User Stories\n    88→\n    89→### STORY-001: ORM Base Infrastructure\n    90→\n    91→**As a** developer\n    92→**I want** SQLAlchemy base classes and type utilities\n    93→**So that** all ORM models have consistent patterns\n    94→\n    95→**Acceptance Criteria:**\n    96→- [ ] `Base` declarative base class with naming conventions\n    97→- [ ] `UUIDMixin` for UUIDv7 primary keys\n    98→- [ ] `TimestampMixin` for `created_at`/`updated_at`\n    99→- [ ] `EnumByValue` type for enum storage by value\n   100→- [ ] Session factory with async support\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6044bc8c-bcbf-48e4-90f1-5ef30954a52d","uuid":"20946deb-a12d-4b30-9721-1e20052f8ce2","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ryan/Work/guitar-tone-worktrees/main/.ralph-hybrid/main/spec.md","content":"---\ncreated: 2026-02-03T03:15:00Z\ngithub_issue: null\nsource: https://github.com/krazyuniks/guitar-tone-shootout/wiki/IMPLEMENTATION\n---\n\n# Phase 3: Adapter Implementation\n\nImplementation of three parallel adapter sub-phases that build on the core domain (Phase 2).\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThe core domain layer (`libs/core/`) defines entities, value objects, and port protocols but has no concrete implementations. Phase 3 delivers the adapter layer:\n\n- **3A (Persistence):** SQLAlchemy ORM models and repository implementations for `gts_core` database\n- **3B (Audio):** Audio processing library implementing the `AudioProcessor` protocol\n- **3C (Frontend):** Astro build system for templates and static assets\n\nThese three sub-phases modify distinct directories and can execute in parallel:\n- 3A: `apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/` and `infrastructure/migrations/`\n- 3B: `libs/audio/src/audio/`\n- 3C: `frontend/astro/`\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] All ORM models with relationships pass protocol compliance tests\n- [ ] Repositories implement all methods from `libs/core/ports/repositories.py`\n- [ ] Alembic migrations create complete `gts_core` schema\n- [ ] Audio processor implements `AudioProcessor` protocol with async support\n- [ ] NAM model loading with LRU caching functional\n- [ ] Loudness normalization (EBU R128) operational\n- [ ] Astro builds successfully to `frontend/astro/dist/`\n- [ ] Tailwind CSS compiles with design tokens\n- [ ] Base Jinja2 wrapper generates valid HTML\n- [ ] Static pages (index, about, login) render correctly\n- [ ] `just check` passes (lint, types, tests)\n- [ ] Wiki documentation updated for all three sub-phases\n\n## Execution Guidelines\n\n### Test-Driven Development (MANDATORY)\n\n**Every story MUST follow Red-Green-Refactor:**\n\n1. **RED - Write failing tests FIRST**\n   - Before writing ANY implementation code, write tests for the story's acceptance criteria\n   - Run the tests - they MUST fail (if they pass, you're not testing new behaviour)\n\n2. **GREEN - Implement to pass**\n   - Write the minimum code to make your tests pass\n   - Run tests frequently during implementation\n\n3. **REFACTOR - Clean up (if needed)**\n   - Improve code quality while keeping tests green\n\n### Archive Reference\n\nArchive code at `../../guitar-tone-worktrees-archive-20260202/main/` provides reference implementations:\n\n| Archive Path | Target | Classification |\n|--------------|--------|----------------|\n| `backend/app/models/*.py` | `apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/models/` | REFACTOR |\n| `backend/app/adapters/persistence/*.py` | `apps/webapp/src/webapp/adapters/persistence/` | REFACTOR |\n| `backend/app/adapters/processing/pedalboard_audio.py` | `libs/audio/src/audio/processing/` | REFACTOR |\n| `backend/app/adapters/processing/nam_loader.py` | `libs/audio/src/audio/processing/` | REFACTOR |\n| `backend/app/adapters/processing/ir_loader.py` | `libs/audio/src/audio/processing/` | REFACTOR |\n| `astro/astro.config.mjs` | `frontend/astro/` | REFACTOR |\n| `astro/src/styles/global.css` | `frontend/astro/src/styles/` | REFACTOR |\n| `astro/src/layouts/` | `frontend/astro/src/layouts/` | REFACTOR |\n| `astro/src/pages/*.astro` | `frontend/astro/src/pages/` | REFACTOR |\n\n### Container Execution\n\nAll commands run in containers via `just`:\n- Backend: `docker compose exec backend <command>`\n- Astro: `just build-astro` or `just watch-astro`\n- Tests: `just tdd <path>`\n\n### Background Agents\n\nUse `Task` tool with `run_in_background: true` for parallel work:\n- `Explore` agent for codebase research\n- `Bash` agent for running tests in background\n\n---\n\n## User Stories\n\n### STORY-001: ORM Base Infrastructure\n\n**As a** developer\n**I want** SQLAlchemy base classes and type utilities\n**So that** all ORM models have consistent patterns\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] `Base` declarative base class with naming conventions\n- [ ] `UUIDMixin` for UUIDv7 primary keys\n- [ ] `TimestampMixin` for `created_at`/`updated_at`\n- [ ] `EnumByValue` type for enum storage by value\n- [ ] Session factory with async support","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":812}}}
